---
const facts = [
  'Weekly ingest of Cook County property records so PINs, addresses, classifications, assessments, and sales don\'t get retyped',
  'Contact and matter sync with the CRM they already used, with signed files written back to the matter',
  'Township appeal-window tracking so a file only moves when that township is actually open',
  'PIN-validated intake with duplicate flags',
  'A three-document retainer packet, e-sign, then split and filed back into the matter',
];
---

<section class="study" id="case-study">
  <div class="study-inner">
    <div class="site-section-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="site-section-title">A Cook County appeal practice, after the spreadsheet years</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="study-layout">
      <div class="study-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="study-lead">
          A property tax appeal firm in Cook County had outgrown their CRM plus
          spreadsheets plus inbox. Volume was fine. The glue work wasn't.
        </p>
        <ul>
          {facts.map((fact) => (
            <li>{fact}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="study-close">
          We are not going to invent a percentage of hours saved. What we can say:
          the clerical path from new client to signed, filed packet no longer
          depends on one person remembering every step.
        </p>
        <a class="btn study-cta" href="#contact" data-scroll-to="contact">Schedule a workflow assessment</a>
      </div>
      <div class="study-media" data-reveal>
        <img
          src="/images/dashboard.png?v=1"
          width="800"
          height="500"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          alt=""
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .study {
    padding: var(--section-pad-y) var(--section-pad-x);
  }

  .study-inner {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .study-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .study-lead {
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.7vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .study-copy ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .study-copy li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--site-text-dim);
  }

  .study-copy li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    background: var(--site-accent);
  }

  .study-close {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--site-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .study-cta {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem 0.75rem 1.45rem;
  }

  .study-media {
    line-height: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--site-border);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .study-media img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4/3;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top left;
    filter: brightness(0.88) contrast(1.05) saturate(0.7);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .study-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.75rem;
    }

    .study-media {
      order: -1;
    }
  }
</style>
